      "subject_asset_id": "skill_bundle:dvaac/03:apply-config@2.0.0",
      "title": "Bundled validation file contains a guarded exec() path for a code block extracted from SKILL.md",
      "description": "tests/apply_payload_demo.py reads SKILL.md, extracts the first python fenced code block, and contains a guarded exec() path that runs when DVAAC_DANGER_RUN_PAYLOAD=1. DVAAC deliberately names the file outside pytest's default discovery pattern and guards payload execution, but the file demonstrates the developer-execution-surface primitive: auxiliary bundle code can execute attacker-controlled content with local user permissions before any agentic release decision is made. The demonstration payload writes a marker file to /tmp/dvaac_hidden_test_payload.txt — deliberately a safe local sink rather than a network exfiltration — so the fixture proves the threat class without performing a real attack. In production, an attacker controlling a validation path like this could substitute any payload: credential reads, network egress, persistence. The declared manifest and declared script are clean; the threat lives entirely in a file outside the declared execution surface.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "evidence://dvaac/03/files/skill/tests/apply_payload_demo.py#L39-L42"
      ],
      "detector": {
        "name": "dvaac.reference.skill-static",
        "version": "0.1.1",
        "rule_id": "DVAAC-SKILL-DEVEXEC-01"
      },
      "remediation": "Reject the skill bundle. Treat the bundle as malicious. Audit any developer machine on which the test suite has been executed.",
      "created_at": "2026-05-14T15:09:30Z"
    }
